 242, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ScienceMagazine/status/2113617189865472497/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113617187285909504", "start": 219, "url": "https://t.co/q6FiDmBO1e"}]}, "id": "2113617189865472497", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 7, "impression_count": 21015, "like_count": 28, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "Science is publishing an Erratum to replace the June 2026 Editorial Expression of Concern for the September 2024 Research Article “Durably reducing conspiracy beliefs through dialogues with AI.” https://t.co/ukD4uoHGW6 https://t.co/q6FiDmBO1e", "url": "https://x.com/ScienceMagazine/status/2113617189865472497"}, {"author_id": "28164923", "created_at": "2026-10-23T13:00:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113616561219031295"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 166, "id": "89043072", "start": 152, "username": "jasonzweigwsj"}], "urls": [{"description": "One of Wall Street’s regulators is pondering changes to the way investors can seek to recover losses.", "display_url": "on.wsj.com/4kdcowg", "end": 190, "expanded_url": "https://on.wsj.com/4kdcowg", "images": [{"height": 640, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113616566474395648/W-uqBiqe?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1280}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113616566474395648/W-uqBiqe?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 167, "status": 200, "title": "Brokerage Firms Want to Yank Away Your Investor Protections", "unwound_url": "https://www.wsj.com/finance/investing/brokerage-firms-want-to-yank-away-your-investor-protections-b9fddd88?reflink=e2twmkts", "url": "https://t.co/78ICzg5kix"}]}, "id": "2113616561219031295", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 9089, "like_count": 42, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "The Intelligent Investor: Regulators may soon decide whether an unlevel playing field should be tilted even more steeply against the little guy, writes @jasonzweig